From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:18:57 +0900
Subject: Make an inline trait's members deferred whichever unit asks first

After pickling, `PruneInlineTraits` empties the definitions of an inline
trait, whose code its children hold, and its symbol transformer makes the
members deferred and the trait one without an initializer. The transformer did
so only if the unit being compiled had specializations; `transformTemplate`
goes by the unit of the trait.

A denotation is transformed once, when it is first asked for at the phase. If
that happened while a unit which only uses the trait was current, one which
neither declares nor extends an inline trait, the members stayed concrete for
the rest of the run, and the backend then met them with their definitions
emptied: "Concrete method has no definition". Whether two files compiled
together depended on their order.

The transformer now goes by the symbol alone. No symbol is an inline trait, or
a member of one, unless inline traits are in use.

Written with LLM assistance (Claude Code); reviewed content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: inlinetraitprune
---
 .../tools/dotc/transform/PruneInlineTraits.scala    | 12 ++++++++----
 tests/pos/inline-trait-used-first/A_1.scala         | 13 +++++++++++++
 tests/pos/inline-trait-used-first/B_1.scala         |  8 ++++++++
 3 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/pos/inline-trait-used-first/A_1.scala
 create mode 100644 tests/pos/inline-trait-used-first/B_1.scala

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/PruneInlineTraits.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/PruneInlineTraits.scala
index 781b60e1b977c71faf264e3a641d0c1cec986124..2a89a75081a97325cdfccfe9c66095b8f0f10205 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/PruneInlineTraits.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/PruneInlineTraits.scala
@@ -21,12 +21,16 @@ class PruneInlineTraits extends MiniPhase with SymTransformer { thisTransform =>
   
   override def runsAfter: Set[String] = Set(PruneInlinedMethods.name)
   
+  /** The members of an inline trait become deferred, and the trait loses its initializer,
+   *  whichever unit is being compiled when the symbol is first asked for: a denotation is
+   *  transformed once, so going by the current unit's `hasSpecializations` left the
+   *  members concrete for good if a unit which merely uses the trait came first, while
+   *  `transformTemplate` still emptied their definitions.
+   */
   override def transformSym(sym: SymDenotation)(using Context): SymDenotation = {
-    val hasSpecializations = ctx.compilationUnit.hasSpecializations
-
-    if hasSpecializations && isEraseable(sym) then 
+    if isEraseable(sym) then 
       sym.copySymDenotation(initFlags = sym.flags | Deferred)
-    else if hasSpecializations && sym.isInlineTrait then
+    else if sym.isClass && sym.isInlineTrait then
       val clsInfo = sym.asClass.classInfo
       val clsInfo2 = clsInfo.derivedClassInfo(decls = 
           clsInfo.decls.filteredScope(!isDeletable(_))
diff --git a/tests/pos/inline-trait-used-first/A_1.scala b/tests/pos/inline-trait-used-first/A_1.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3a727b72bce3e29c9370efa1f2eb9ed7b7022711
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/pos/inline-trait-used-first/A_1.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+//> using options -experimental -language:experimental.inlineTraits
+
+// The two files are compiled together, this one first. It only uses the inline trait,
+// so its unit has no specializations, and the trait's members were first transformed
+// while it was the current unit: they stayed concrete, though the definitions were
+// emptied in the trait's own unit. "Concrete method has no definition: def run(): Unit".
+
+package app
+
+object Reader:
+  def count(counter: lib.Counter[Byte]): Int =
+    counter.advance()
+    counter.count
diff --git a/tests/pos/inline-trait-used-first/B_1.scala b/tests/pos/inline-trait-used-first/B_1.scala
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4ebe264292ab2ea81c54e44d299b2654bae7035b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/pos/inline-trait-used-first/B_1.scala
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+//> using options -experimental -language:experimental.inlineTraits
+
+package lib
+
+inline trait Counter[operand]:
+  var count: Int = 1
+
+  def advance(): Unit = count = count + count
